Citations, written before a line of any of them is implemented
--------------------------------------------------------------

This section is not boilerplate and it is not written after the fact. It names
the published sources this library implements from, and it is checked by
Ft8DeepNoticeTests in tests/Ft8Sharp.Deep.Tests, because a NOTICE nothing checks
is a NOTICE that will rot the first time somebody tidies it.

Ordered statistics decoding - PHASE_PLAN.md step 2:

    M. P. C. Fossorier and S. Lin, "Soft-Decision Decoding of Linear Block
    Codes Based on Ordered Statistics," IEEE Transactions on Information
    Theory, vol. 41, no. 5, pp. 1379-1396, September 1995

The protocol itself:

    Franke K9AN, Somerville G4WJS, Taylor K1JT, "The FT4 and FT8 Communication
    Protocols," QEX, July/August 2020

As of this version neither is implemented. Ft8DeepSlotDecoder delegates to
Ft8Sharp and returns exactly what the port returns. The citations are here first
so that when the algorithms arrive there is no moment at which the code exists
and the credit does not.

Where the algorithms come from, and where they do not
-----------------------------------------------------

Everything this library implements comes from published description.

No WSJT-X source was read, and no ft4_ft8_public/ was read. That is a standing
ruling of this phase and it is not a matter of preference: a decoder written from
somebody else's source is a derivative of it, and this one is not. Where an
algorithm is needed, it is written from the papers cited above and from public
literature, and the source is cited at the point of use in the code as well as
here.

ft8_lib by Karlis Goba (https://github.com/kgoba/ft8_lib) is the ancestor of
Ft8Sharp and its debt is acknowledged in that library's own NOTICE. It is not the
ancestor of anything in Ft8Sharp.Deep, and it is the thing this library is trying
to improve on rather than a source it draws from.

